# ArduRover defaults for LEVIA_H7. Embedded by scripts/build-rover.sh.
# Matches src/devkit_mavlink_bridge/mavlink.md in Agroecology-Lab/Sowbot.

# --- Serial ports ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Not the board defaults: the hwdef puts RC on SERIAL2 and a second GPS on SERIAL5.
# ArduPilot gives GPS1 to the lowest-numbered port set to GPS, so the base F9P must
# stay on SERIAL2 and the rover F9P on SERIAL3. Swapping them breaks the moving baseline.
#   SERIAL2 = USART6, U8   F9P #1 (base, GPS1)
#   SERIAL3 = USART2, U24  F9P #2 (rover, GPS2)
#   SERIAL5 = UART4,  U20  Avaota SBC, MAVLink2 (devkit_mavlink_bridge)
# U8 no longer carries an RC receiver on this vehicle.
SERIAL2_PROTOCOL 5
SERIAL3_PROTOCOL 5
SERIAL5_PROTOCOL 2
# 115 is 115200 baud. Must match MAVLINK_BAUD on the SBC (bridge default 115200).
SERIAL5_BAUD 115

# --- GNSS and heading -----------------------------------------------------------
# Heading from two F9P receivers (moving baseline). ArduPilot routes the RTCM3 from the
# base to the rover itself, so there is no UART2 wire between the receivers.
GPS_TYPE 17
GPS_TYPE2 18
GPS_AUTO_CONFIG 1
# Yaw from GPS, with compass fallback.
EK3_SRC1_YAW 3
# Set GPS_MB1_OFS_X/Y/Z to the base-to-rover antenna offset in metres once
# the antennas are fixed to the vehicle, and check the sign on the bench.

# --- Failsafes ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both stop the rover in place (Hold, FS_ACTION 2), not RTL.
# SBC or bridge dead: the bridge sends a ground-station HEARTBEAT every 1 s, so the GCS
# failsafe fires FS_GCS_TIMEOUT seconds after it stops. 2 s is the lowest value allowed.
FS_ACTION 2
FS_GCS_ENABLE 1
FS_GCS_TIMEOUT 2
# EKF unhealthy or GNSS lost: variance failsafe, threshold left at the default 0.8.
FS_EKF_ACTION 1
# Fence breach: Hold, not the default RTL or Hold. FENCE_ENABLE is left off here: the
# boundary is site specific, so load it and enable the fence when commissioning.
FENCE_ACTION 2
#
# Guided-mode stop. mavlink.md lists GUID_TIMEOUT ~1 s as a second layer behind the bridge's
# own zero-on-stale. Rover has no GUID_TIMEOUT at the pinned ArduPilot commit
# (ardupilot/UPSTREAM_COMMIT): it stops a guided target after a fixed 3 s, about 4.8 m at
# 1.6 m/s. Only ArduPilot master has the parameter. Until the pin moves, the bridge's
# cmd_vel_timeout_s (0.5 s) is the only fast stop.
